<code>assert !Objects.isNull(coll) => this.containsAll(coll) && this.size() == coll.size();</code>

This assert statement checks that if the input collection `coll` is not null, then the constructed `TreeList` contains all elements of `coll` and has the same size as `coll`.
--------------------
<code>assert CollectionUtils.isEqualCollection(this, coll);</code>

However, since we need to use only publicly accessible observer methods provided in the test function and avoid calling the constructor directly, we should compare the elements one by one. Here's the correct assert statement:

<code>assert this.size() == coll.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(coll.toArray()[i]);</code>
